      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 10.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>For \\( f(x)=x^{2}-2 \\), between which integers does a root lie?</p>\\[ 1\\ \\text{and}\\ 2,\\ \\text{since}\\ f(1)&lt;0&lt;f(2). \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Newton-Raphson",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Use Newton-Raphson to find the root of \\(f(x)=x^3-5\\) near \\(x_0=1.7\\). Do one iteration.</p><p>\\(f(x)=x^3-5\\), \\(f'(x)=3x^2\\).</p>\\[x_1=x_0-\\frac{f(x_0)}{f'(x_0)}=1.7-\\frac{1.7^3-5}{3(1.7)^2}=1.7-\\frac{4.913-5}{8.67}=1.7-\\frac{-0.087}{8.67}\\approx1.710.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example C — Algebraic Structure & Vieta's Root Relations",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve the quadratic equation \\( x^2 - 13x + 36 = 0 \\) and verify the sum and product of its roots.<br><br><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br><ol><li>Factor into binomials: \\( (x - 4)(x - 9) = 0 \\implies x = 4 \\text{ or } x = 9 \\).</li><li>Check Vieta's formulas: sum \\( = 4 + 9 = \\mathbf{13} \\) and product \\( = (4)(9) = \\mathbf{36} \\).</li></ol>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked Example D — Algebraic Structure & Vieta's Root Relations",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Solve the quadratic equation \\( x^2 - 10x + 25 = 0 \\) and verify the sum and product of its roots.<br><br><strong>Step-by-step Solution:</strong><br><ol><li>Factor into binomials: \\( (x - 5)(x - 5) = 0 \\implies x = 5 \\text{ or } x = 5 \\).</li><li>Check Vieta's formulas: sum \\( = 5 + 5 = \\mathbf{10} \\) and product \\( = (5)(5) = \\mathbf{25} \\).</li></ol>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Show that \\(x^3+2x-6=0\\) has a root in \\([1,2]\\). Taking \\(x_0=1.5\\), perform one Newton-Raphson iteration.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(f(1)=-3&lt;0\\), \\(f(2)=6&gt;0\\): sign change confirms root. \\(f(1.5)=1.5^3+3-6=-0.625\\). \\(f'(x)=3x^2+2\\Rightarrow f'(1.5)=8.75\\). \\(x_1=1.5-\\tfrac{-0.625}{8.75}\\approx1.571\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "figure",
        "figure": {
          "type": "fn",
          "fns": [
            {
